# SamRenderer.gd
# Converts allophone frames (from SamParser) into a mono PCM byte buffer.
#
# Algorithm overview (SAM-inspired, clean-room):
#   For each allophone frame:
#     1. Generate a buzz source at the current pitch (voiced) or white noise (unvoiced).
#     2. Run the source through two simple one-pole resonators tuned to F1 and F2
#        formant frequencies derived from the phoneme table.
#     3. Mix voiced/unvoiced components according to the phoneme's voicing flag.
#     4. Apply crunch (bit-depth quantisation) if requested.
#     5. Accumulate samples into the output buffer.
#
# The mouth/throat parameters in the voice profile shift F2 and F1 respectively,
# providing the "character" controls familiar from SAM.
class_name SamRenderer
extends RefCounted

